# /sdd-design

Purpose:
  Design analysis and skill invocation. Supports manual trigger and
  automatic invocation based on task context.

Owns: commands/sdd-design.sdd

Description:
  Analyzes design quality, invokes design skills, and evaluates
  implementations against design best practices. Can be triggered
  manually or automatically when design-related work is detected.

Usage:
  /sdd-design
  /sdd-design --generate
  /sdd-design --evaluate
  /sdd-design --discover
  /sdd-design --review <path>
  /sdd-design --manual
  /sdd-design --auto

Options:
  --generate  Run Unified Design Intelligence pipeline (Stages 1-7) —
              brief → tokens (DESIGN.md) → structure → components →
              style → verify → review. The ONLY sanctioned UI generation path.
  --evaluate  Run design quality evaluation
  --discover  Discover missing design skills
  --review    Review design implementation at path
  --manual    Force manual mode (no auto-invoke)
  --auto      Force auto-invoke mode

Mode: READ_ONLY (evaluate/discover) | READ_WRITE (review/generate)

InitialLoad (Phase 151 — EXPAND protocol):
  - .sdd/INDEX.sdd (routing only)
  - .sdd/skills/design/intelligence/INDEX.sdd (pipeline + gates)
  - active DESIGN.md for the target (if exists)
  Native design skills, sources registry, imported references load on EXPAND only.

Subcommands:
  generate    Run Unified Design Intelligence pipeline on a design brief
  evaluate    Analyze design quality against .sdd/skills/design/*
  discover    Find gaps in design skill coverage
  review      Review code/design against design principles
  apply       Apply design skill to current context

Output:
  DESIGN EVALUATION

    Overall Score: <0-100>
    Category Scores:
      Taste:           <0-100>
      Heuristics:      <0-100>
      Visual:          <0-100>
      UX:              <0-100>
      Accessibility:   <0-100>
      Design System:   <0-100>

    Decision: <PASS | WARN | BLOCK>

  Issues:
    [<severity>] <category>: <description>
      Recommendation: <action>

Rules:
  [DSN-01] /sdd-design MUST NOT modify code in evaluate mode.
  [DSN-02] /sdd-design MUST produce @design.* evaluation records.
  [DSN-03] /sdd-design discover MUST recommend skills with >= 80% relevance.
  [DSN-04] /sdd-design MUST integrate with skill auto-invocation.
  [DSN-05] /sdd-design MUST respect DESIGN.md as source of truth.
  [DSN-06] /sdd-design MUST check WCAG 2.1 AA baseline for accessibility.
  [DSN-07] /sdd-design --generate MUST follow the intelligence pipeline
           (design/intelligence/INDEX.sdd) — SlopGates both at tokens and
           verify stages; freeform generation is BLOCKED.
  [DSN-08] /sdd-design --generate MUST run drift enforcement on subsequent
           related work ([DI9]).

